# CODEOWNERS — automatic code review assignment
#
# GitHub uses this file to request reviews from the right people when a PR
# touches files under these paths. Add team names as @org/team or individual
# users as @username.
#
# This repository has a single maintainer (cromstel is a User, not an org), so
# every path resolves to the same owner. The section headers below document
# which areas are considered sensitive; they are not separate reviewers. Code
# owner review is disabled in the branch ruleset, so these entries are
# informational groupings rather than a merge gate.

# Global catch-all — the maintainer reviews everything by default
* @cromstel

# Security-sensitive paths
**/.github/** @cromstel
**/lib/api/auth.ts @cromstel
**/lib/utils/crypto.ts @cromstel
**/lib/utils/encryption.ts @cromstel
**/lib/services/authService.ts @cromstel

# Database layer
**/lib/db/** @cromstel

# Frontend/UI
**/app/(app)/** @cromstel
**/components/** @cromstel

# API routes
**/app/api/** @cromstel

# Infrastructure/deployment
**/.github/workflows/cd.yml @cromstel
**/docker-compose.yml @cromstel
**/Dockerfile @cromstel
